    {
      "id": "cell-39",
      "source": [
        "I = list(range(X.shape[0]))\n",
        "np.random.shuffle( I )\n",
        "\n",
        "I_train = I[:60]\n",
        "I_valid = I[60:]\n",
        "\n",
        "X_train = X.iloc[I_train, : ]\n",
        "y_train = y.iloc[I_train]\n",
        "\n",
        "X_valid = X.iloc[I_valid, : ]\n",
        "y_valid = y.iloc[I_valid]"
      ],
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": [],
      "metadata": {
        "attributes": {
          "classes": [
            "This tutorial is designed to equip you with essential knowledge and skills in Machine Learning, setting a strong foundation for exploring advanced topics such as Deep Learning."
          ],
          "id": ""
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "cell-40",
      "source": "<p>We now to train the model with 200 <code style=\"color: inherit\">alpha</code> values logarithmically spaced between \\(10^{−3}\\) and \\(10^2\\) with L1 penalty (Lasso regression) and make prediction on both the train and validation sets:</p>\n",
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "editable": false,
        "collapsed": false
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "cell-41",
      "source": [
        "logalphas = []\n",
        "\n",
        "r2_train = []\n",
        "r2_valid = []\n",
        "\n",
        "for alpha in np.logspace(-3, 2, 200):\n",
        "    reg = SGDRegressor(penalty=\"l1\", alpha=alpha)\n",
        "    reg.fit(X_train, y_train)\n",
        "\n",
        "    logalphas.append(np.log10(alpha))\n",
        "    r2_train.append(r2_score(y_train, reg.predict(X_train)))\n",
        "    r2_valid.append(r2_score(y_valid, reg.predict(X_valid)))"
      ],
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": [],
      "metadata": {
        "attributes": {
          "classes": [
            "This tutorial is designed to equip you with essential knowledge and skills in Machine Learning, setting a strong foundation for exploring advanced topics such as Deep Learning."
          ],
          "id": ""
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "cell-42",
      "source": "<p>Let’s visualize the \\(R^2\\) for both the train and validation sets, as well as the \\(\\alpha\\) value with highest \\(R^2\\) for the validation set:</p>\n",
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "editable": false,
        "collapsed": false
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "cell-43",
      "source": [
        "bestI = np.argmax(r2_valid)\n",
        "bestLogAlpha = logalphas[bestI]\n",
        "bestR2_valid = r2_valid[bestI]\n",
        "\n",
        "fig,ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(10,5))\n",
        "fig.suptitle(f\"best alpha : {10**bestLogAlpha:.2f} - validation R2 : {bestR2_valid:.2f}\")\n",
        "ax.plot(logalphas, r2_train, label=\"train set\")\n",
        "ax.plot(logalphas, r2_valid, label=\"validation set\")\n",
        "ax.scatter([bestLogAlpha], [bestR2_valid], c=\"red\")\n",
        "ax.set_xlabel(\"log10( alpha )\")\n",
        "ax.set_ylabel(\"R2\")\n",
        "ax.set_ylim(-0.1, 1.1)\n",
        "ax.legend()"
      ],
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": [],
