5x/XeQ3JzzAhjZcQ0P3\nWu1NU9sTj9Xe3XnBxRzGUT1Kg/qVOYzNByu41HXU4AitmOXtiAzpVFJgCBcM\nMHIshvgoms7omTFkGwbmRqs54U742vkIpmIIN77t58ZsPCsOehVbEmutZ+V5\nObhB6zhHc1RReBQOaajgAjobL8QQynXoXtRtef8xwfgScgwuEuMGRtyc3o/o\nHWalbIivIY5u9dUIo87WNkNnW2VN1Egs3jCGlGSQtXQ5wXU5xMWNRjiI2DAj\nog2BAfQE+pdleYffCJIiFI5X1cYug6WiMyZFw11PTkxaPDOoFZ6I20ZKhWRE\nh5URtRWXDa/vYUMIv7YZwuSEGoXs9rDLIznfT5qeCK1C+gNjqGmm1NTZRuwD\n4QATfz4JNOgbt8+M8sZSEmjF+eVpcXuToa3d7XaqNphsiAwhGwNDcD/P3MP4\nPP0dVA7jFRzGK3cYL4m3fz/2nCFn6M+myBn6Ca/39vZ/5699/IFeucNwOBwO\nxy/7HS9JORwOh+NX4E1vh8PhcPxaiuFjtQ6Hw+FwOBwOh8PhcDgcDofD4XA4\nHA6Hw+FwOBwOh8PhcDgcDsffhf8BFMiGFC3wRF8AAAAASUVORK5CYII=\n\"\" alt=\"Customized multi-plot. \" width=\"1584\" height=\"1296\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n<blockquote class=\"question\" style=\"border: 2px solid #8A9AD0; margin: 1em 0.2em\">\n<div class=\"box-title question-title\" id=\"question-pm2-5-over-italy\"><i class=\"far fa-question-circle\" aria-hidden=\"true\" ></i> Question: PM2.5 over Italy</div>\n<p>Using a Multi-plot between Rome and Naples, can you tell us if the forecasted PM2.5 will increase or decrease during the first 24 hours?</p>\n<br/><details style=\"border: 2px solid #B8C3EA; margin: 1em 0.2em;padding: 0.5em; cursor: pointer;\"><summary>👁 View solution</summary>\n<div class=\"box-title solution-title\" id=\"solution-2\"><button class=\"gtn-boxify-button solution\" type=\"button\" aria-controls=\"solution-2\" aria-expanded=\"true\"><i class=\"far fa-eye\" aria-hidden=\"true\" ></i> <span>Solution</span><span class=\"fold-unfold fa fa-minus-square\"></span></button></div>\n<p>We will select a sub-area: 11. East to 15.0 East and 40. N to 43. N. PM2.5 will increase and reach values close to 35 μm.m-3.\nWe will use <code style=\"color: inherit\">slice</code> to select the area and we slice latitudes with <code style=\"color: inherit\">latitude=slice(47.3, 36.5)</code> and not <code style=\"color: inherit\">latitude=slice(36.5, 47.3)</code>.\nThe reason is that when using slice, you need to specify values using the same order as in the coordinates. Latitudes are specified in\ndecreasing order for CAMS.</p>\n<blockquote class=\"code-in\" style=\"border: 2px solid #86D486; margin: 1em 0.2em\">\n<div class=\"box-title code-in-title\" id=\"code-in-python-2\"><i class=\"far fa-keyboard\" aria-hidden=\"true\" ></i> Code In: Python</div>\n<div class=\"language-plaintext highlighter-rouge\"><div><pre style=\"color: inherit; background: transparent\"><code style=\"color: inherit\">fig = plt.figure(1, figsize=[10,10])\n\n# We're using cartopy to project our data.\n# (see documentation on cartopy)\nproj_plot = ccrs.Mercator()\n\n# We need to project our data to the new projection and for this we use &lt;code&gt;transform&lt;/code&gt;.\n# we set the original data projection in transform (here PlateCarree)\np = dset.sel(time=slice(np.timedelta64(1,'h'),np.timedelta64(1,'D'))).sel(latitude=slice(43., 40.),\n                                                                          longitude=slice(11.,15.))['pm2p5_conc'].plot(transform=ccrs.PlateCarree(),\n                                                                                     vmin = 0, vmax = 35,\n                                                                                     subplot_kws={\"projection\": proj_plot},\n                                                                                     col='time', col_wrap=4,\n                                                                                     robust=True,\n                                                                                     aspect=dset.dims[\"longitude\"] / dset.dims[\"latitude\"],  # for a sensible figsize\n                                                                                     cmap=cmc.roma_r)\n# We have to set the map's options on all axes\nfor ax,i in zip(p.axes.flat,  (np.datetime64('2021-12-22') + dset.time.sel(time=slice(np.timedelta64(0),np.timedelta64(1,'D')))).values):\n    ax.coastlines('10m')\n    ax.set_title(\"CAMS PM2.5 \" + pd.to_datetime(i).strftime(\"%d %b %H:%S UTC\"), fontsize=12)\n# Save your figure\nplt.savefig(\"CAMS-PM2_5-fc-multi-Italy.png\")\n</code></pre></div>      </div>\n</details>\n<p><img src=\"data:image/png;base64,iVBORw0KGgoAAAANSUhEUgAABjAAAAUQCAMAAADd/elnAAABwlBMVEVMaXEA\nAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAACAQEAAAAAAAAAAAAlc7Urhb0qgrsmdrct\niL4ia7InebgjbrMhaLAwkMFRt9FXvNIpf7ozlcMkcbQpfrkofLk/pcouir85\nnsc2mcU8oskgZa8vjL9DqsxMs88wjcBjxdVGrc1oyNVtzNZyz9bL6LO/6sV/\n1tcfYK140te56skyksKF2deK29fH6rrD6sCP3tc1l8SZ4taU4NbO5quj5dSe\n5NWw6c84nMaq59JJsM5Bp8scWKm06s1+FwBgwtRdwdPS0X7S1odbv9MJGybR\n4qB71NfRzHXQ5KW2jTLS25LDp0et6NDOwme9mjvS3pecVxemah+QQA2m5tKv\nfimzhS3AoUHPx26WTBOhYhyJMQi6lDfMvWAYTqXLuVzJtVcRJizS2Y3HsVIJ\nDxDR35urdSXGrU2CJQSpcCIgLisRQZ8INpsIFh8WNUUsLh+teSYbR1skXXMk\nGAs3V1VVTShbaFAhY45MHwc1coATQXhVfHQ1fpMmcp5OpLWGcjJjnpyKi1dK\nj5mCsaBls7ikqGs+la99wr00hqJ7ln2Zsoyyx5QpfKwxirGU0cGt1bPkhHSg\nAAAADHRSTlMAfCdc5Y8PzfpBu6Qp+lxOAAAACXBIWXMAAAsTAAALEwEAmpwY\nAAAgAElEQVR42uy9iV8bR7b+DZilvSZxbBwnYTAOjMHsweCFeMWxsRU7N5Pc\nSeI7Yycz/G57Oncy+ny6ebsREFmYYCAs3vh/3zpPd59Wa0PCUquE6ggbSWjr\no1Pn20/VqaqGBmXKlClTpkyZMmXKlClTpkyZMmXKlClTpkyZMmXKlClTpkyZ\nMmXKlClTpkyZMmXKlClTpkyZMmXKlClTpkyZMmXKlClTpuxd7ECb1nzoIF3R\nDoj/D2qHxf9N2iHvL0140GENVxu1RnGD/j94qLn5cKv7Coc08Vf36kHxFLq7\npVlrO+DdRX89fDDne4uH4w1amptbvLuaDmlt+DTN2iHv9TV6SOPhA5pr4r21\nZv/V68NBdMQNykH5HdQontUorYOk8FCzJnEbU1Yz1th8oLXhIIXSoeZDFF/N\nzQjGQyKgDza0HvCCubGh9XCbeHCbuNEm2ubBA62thw95wRwE1oGDra2HxIs1\nNokXcgP4oIjzpkYtVzS3agdaW9oocJta/ehsa2k9oLXSm7cePhwKZu+1ROto\nFH8/XE8OOnjgAANDOSiHg8Sjm5pljSApPNTU2tB6qFFWDymrFWvV/Ehs0iiI\nRLy0iHuaGw+Jk5/gYSKYRRCJiGoTLbPtcKP3jKxgdk+nvLsbOZhF66CYFWdM\n4qGtdGrU6j+yVYQqwcJ7VhN9BvGCLYe969nB3NZSdw7yH6QclNdB4gEtcjpI\nGg8BM1J6SFnN2EGNT4PaGtooZJsPtglBeoDOfloOtgbBTCc7jYcbWxpaGr1g\nbvSjtrm5Le3kpsU9MWlNO/uh92ltFZHc1NzU0CJk8MGgiQta0KkRtQwR/mgJ\n4n60BC8ThIO5VTtYdw7yH6QclNdB7i8ZHSSJh0Rvk/iDnB5SVjMWdHUIDUzR\nKeKluenwARHMDQcPN2teH6rfv3q4CX9GMDd50dogQv6AF3cIOE9hH2pIC2Zx\nJkMvKVpCQ