    },
    {
      "id": "cell-30",
      "source": "<p>The expression (70,) tells us we have an N×1 vector, so this is the average inflammation per day for all patients. If we average across axis 1 (columns in our 2D example), we get the average inflammation per patient across all days.:</p>\n",
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "editable": false,
        "collapsed": false
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "cell-31",
      "source": [
        "print(np.mean(random_data, axis=1))"
      ],
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": [],
