    },
    {
      "id": "cell-14",
      "source": "<blockquote class=\"details\" style=\"border: 2px solid #ddd; margin: 1em 0.2em\">\n<div class=\"box-title details-title\" id=\"details-any-problems-with-get-function\"><button class=\"gtn-boxify-button details\" type=\"button\" aria-controls=\"details-any-problems-with-get-function\" aria-expanded=\"true\"><i class=\"fas fa-info-circle\" aria-hidden=\"true\" ></i> <span>Details: Any problems with *get()* function?</span><span class=\"fold-unfold fa fa-minus-square\"></span></button></div>\n<p>There shouldn’t be any issues with fetching data from your Galaxy history using <em>get()</em> function. However, if you experience any problems, you can use the code below to download the input data and be able to follow the tutorial.</p>\n<div class=\"language-plaintext highlighter-rouge\"><div><pre style=\"color: inherit; background: transparent\"><code style=\"color: inherit\">%%bash\nwget -nv https://zenodo.org/records/13743145/files/Filtered_anndata.h5ad\n</code></pre></div>  </div>\n<div class=\"language-plaintext highlighter-rouge\"><div><pre style=\"color: inherit; background: transparent\"><code style=\"color: inherit\">adata = sc.read_h5ad(\"Filtered_anndata.h5ad\")\n</code></pre></div>  </div>\n</blockquote>\n<h2 id=\"draw-force-directed-graph\">Draw force-directed graph</h2>\n<p>First, we will calculate a <a href=\"https://scanpy.readthedocs.io/en/stable/api/scanpy.tl.draw_graph.html\">force-directed graph</a>, as an alternate to tSNE, which will likely work better for trajectory analysis.</p>\n",
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "editable": false,
        "collapsed": false
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "cell-15",
      "source": [
