      "id": "cell-28",
      "source": "<p>If we are happy with those thresholds for cells and percent mito, we can look at the the gene count threshold next.</p>\n<blockquote class=\"comment\" style=\"border: 2px solid #ffecc1; margin: 1em 0.2em\">\n<div class=\"box-title comment-title\" id=\"comment-otherwise\"><i class=\"far fa-comment-dots\" aria-hidden=\"true\" ></i> Comment: Otherwise</div>\n<p>If not, repeat the preceding steps to hone in on a threshold more suited to your needs.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>To set a threshold for gene count, let’s plot the gene counts (nFeature_RNA) against the percent mito (perc.mt):</p>\n",
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "editable": false,
        "collapsed": false
      }
    },
