rL3GgygBqgRoxfJD88M1LfPH+hg\n7PK29fD6MkdBTWruh8fHx4en1qUxKAOoAWrEGMRrmwmcvZKETEGd+vDc+iBS\nUJ8/L6a06dgjQA1QI8YoyHJ6kc7AyOqKgpoU3WQZTUH98KQtpc/bi5cANUCN\nGKNYIIJIiTZlgDJQ39JVNQE1+zf77y/P5wA1QI0Yr4BnGUCNQCAAasREhHS7\n2NIDUuMANWIi4vLciAX8MABqBAIBUCMQCIAagUAA1AgEQI1AIABqBAIBUCMQ\nCIAagUAA1AgEQI1AIABqBAIBUCMQCIAagUAA1AgEQI1AIMYe1AtzCARiUmKB\ngjqJQCAmKv4f9PvxyjTpOZsAAAAASUVORK5CYII=\n\"\" alt=\"DimPlot colored by 0.5 resolution cluster. \" width=\"980\" height=\"708\" loading=\"lazy\" /><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../images/scrna-SeuratRStudio/plot10.png\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><small>Open image in new tab</small></a><br /><br /><figcaption><span class=\"figcaption-prefix\"><strong>Figure 13</strong>:</span> DimPlot colored by 0.5 resolution cluster.</figcaption></figure>\n<blockquote class=\"comment\" style=\"border: 2px solid #ffecc1; margin: 1em 0.2em\">\n<div class=\"box-title comment-title\" id=\"comment-on-cluster-numbering\"><i class=\"far fa-comment-dots\" aria-hidden=\"true\" ></i> Comment: On Cluster Numbering</div>\n<p>Note that Seurat’s cluster numbering is based on size alone, so clusters 0 and 1 are not necessarily related, they are just the clusters containing the most cells.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>It would be nice to know what these cells are. This analysis (googling all of the marker genes, both checking where the ones you know are and then going through marker tables we generated) is an adventurous task for any individual experiment, so we’re going to speed past that and nab the assessment from the original paper!</p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Clusters</th>\n<th>Markers</th>\n<th>Cell Type</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>3</td>\n<td>Il2ra</td>\n<td>Double negative (early T-cell)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>1,2,5</td>\n<td>Cd8b1, Cd8a, Cd4</td>\n<td>Double positive (middle T-cell)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>0</td>\n<td>Cd8b1, Cd8a, Cd4 - high</td>\n<td>Double positive (late middle T-cell)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>4</td>\n<td>Itm2a</td>\n<td>Mature T-cell</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>Feel free to plot these markers onto our dataset to see where they fall. This is generally a useful method of discerning cell types and can be useful for initial annotations.</p>\n<blockquote class=\"tip\" style=\"border: 2px solid #FFE19E; margin: 1em 0.2em\">\n<div class=\"box-title tip-title\" id=\"tip-plotting-markers\"><button class=\"gtn-boxify-button tip\" type=\"button\" aria-controls=\"tip-plotting-markers\" aria-expanded=\"true\"><i class=\"far fa-lightbulb\" aria-hidden=\"true\" ></i> <span>Tip: Plotting Markers</span><span class=\"fold-unfold fa fa-minus-square\"></span></button></div>\n<p>To do so, simply use the same FeaturePlot() function we used above, but replace the feature parameter with your new marker of interest.</p>\n<div class=\"language-plaintext highlighter-rouge\"><div><pre style=\"color: inherit; background: transparent\"><code style=\"color: inherit\">FeaturePlot(object = filtered_srt, features = c(\"Il2ra\", \"Cd8b1\", \"Cd8a\", \"Cd4\", \"Itm2a\"), order = T, ncol = 3)\n</code></pre></div>  </div>\n<figure id=\"figure-14\" style=\"max-width: 90%;\"><img src=\"data:image/png;base64,iVBORw0KGgoAAAANSUhEUgAABW0AAAJrCAMAAACst0ESAAAAqFBMVEX////p\n6er6+vrl5eXa29v4+Pry8vLT09P9/f7W1tYBAQHi4uLt7e2tjue3nuO8peLf\n39+fe+zPy9bFt9zArd729fZUVFSNZfFpaWng1/Ly7vxtRPiVbvC0mOkcHByl\nhO06OjqsrKzPwPB4eHi9vb3KwNnMzMzZy/d8UvWDWvPAqu5bNfrJt+gfM/+V\nlZWFhYVFNf3o4PmioqLs5vbVzePFsveskfRkZPwAzhvSAAAACXBIWXMAAAsS\nAAALEgHS3X78AAAgAElEQVR42uxdDUPiSNMkn0xMgPARIJEARjDK8uAiwvv/\n/9lb3TMJCcKqt7hnbjO7d4uI7h3jVDrV1VWNRr3qVa961etrl2lZVv0u1Kte\n9apXjbb1qle96lWjbb3qVa961atG23rVq171qtG2XvWqV71qtK1XvepVr3rV\naFuvetWrXjXa1qte9apXvWq0rVe96lWvGm3rVa961atG23rVq171qleNtvWq\nV73qVaNtvepVr3rVq0bbetWrXvWq0fZ3l3Y/frEbd+OxgQ/8zXi8MUS925Vb\n1uJ+OB9u3PwJ+2W88RsN/eF5fH/nyY+Pn22Ixfi5Wb9t320J/xnb+PxwfMbb\njJ/xvEYn06/Rtur/X9ObsdZ4nt44jcbd9AZrutDrH/uKLfeet+5mvsguld74\nZvjQsDb8/LDZMPCxc/yCxRyvrd+3b7YCeQJvps95xWMMb+YN8aBOZo22/xm0\nxcPp/Xh6M/frn/tqLU